program param_reassign

? Function parameters are mutable locals: assigning to one stores into
? the local (C by-value semantics — the caller never sees it). This used
? to emit a fresh C declaration that collided with the parameter.

@ bump |n:int| int:
	n = n + 1
	return n
$

@ main ||:
	expected: []
	expected.push|"5"|
	expected.push|"6"|

	x: 5
	y: bump|x|
	print|x|
	print|y|
	print|expected|
$
